From 1b285a84f9cfbe38f3bc6bc5065d60a9ddbab2bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Markuss Broks <markuss.broks@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:52:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] mfd: sm5703: Add support for the Silicon Mitus SM5703
 PMIC

Silicon Mitus SM5703 is a PMIC designed for mobile phones. It contains
LDO, buck, USB LDO and VBUS regulators, a battery charger, a flash LED
driver, a fuel gauge and a MUIC. The MUIC and the fuel gauge have their
own I2C addresses and drivers, while the charger, LED driver and
regulators share the main I2C address handled here.

This is the v5 submission from April 2022 [1], adapted to 6.12:
 - i2c probe() takes only the client
 - the MRSTB line is described as an active-low reset and only released,
   never pulsed, so a running chip is not reset underneath the bootloader
   settings
 - the USB LDO enable bits live in the control register 0x0C, not in the
   LDO3 register 0x1C (cross-checked with the downstream driver)

[1] https://lkml.iu.edu/2204.2/09434.html

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
